1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,967
This is the synthetic card dispute workbench from team bob the builder, for Track Three, Reasoning Architecture.

2
00:00:06,967 --> 00:00:13,524
It connects source evidence to policy, a model proposal, independent validation, and an auditable simulated decision.

3
00:00:13,524 --> 00:00:18,031
This edited walkthrough uses real application captures and dated test evidence.

4
00:00:18,031 --> 00:00:20,900
All records and financial effects are fictional.

5
00:00:21,300 --> 00:00:23,853
Zetaris supplies fresh facts and policy.

6
00:00:23,853 --> 00:00:27,682
One investigator uses Nightshift to propose a structured outcome.

7
00:00:27,682 --> 00:00:30,235
A deterministic critic checks that proposal.

8
00:00:30,235 --> 00:00:33,213
The controller permits at most one correction.

9
00:00:33,213 --> 00:00:42,147
Before any action, the restricted PostgreSQL service rechecks the source and commits the decision, effect, audit, and any review entry atomically.

10
00:00:42,147 --> 00:00:44,700
Confirmed results can then enter memory.

11
00:00:45,100 --> 00:00:49,387
Here is an actual live recovery of case D P fourteen.

12
00:00:49,387 --> 00:00:55,232
Its original source snapshot contains a hundred dollar capture and a forty dollar merchant refund.

13
00:00:55,232 --> 00:00:59,129
The accepted result is a sixty Singapore dollar simulated credit.

14
00:00:59,129 --> 00:01:04,196
Recovery returns the same saved decision and credit identifiers, with zero model calls.

15
00:01:04,196 --> 00:01:08,482
The interface separates the proposal's critic verdict from the persistence result.

16
00:01:08,482 --> 00:01:11,600
Repeated recovery does not create another effective credit.

17
00:01:12,000 --> 00:01:16,786
Next, we select case D P twenty nine and start a new live investigation.

18
00:01:16,786 --> 00:01:19,863
Its claim is one hundred and thirty Singapore dollars.

19
00:01:19,863 --> 00:01:25,333
The application reads the case through Zetaris and selects policy version one from the opening time.

20
00:01:25,733 --> 00:01:28,384
The workbench shows the investigation in progress.

21
00:01:28,384 --> 00:01:32,927
The source policy places this case outside its thirty day filing window.

22
00:01:32,927 --> 00:01:37,850
A valid decline still needs a correctly structured proposal and a confirmed commit.

23
00:01:37,850 --> 00:01:40,500
The running screen reports no financial effect.

24
00:01:40,900 --> 00:01:45,101
In this actual run, Nightshift returned an invalid proposal schema.

25
00:01:45,101 --> 00:01:48,042
The application stopped before critique or persistence.

26
00:01:48,042 --> 00:01:50,563
No decision or credit was created.

27
00:01:50,563 --> 00:01:54,764
A model failure does not invent a human review entry.

28
00:01:54,764 --> 00:01:56,865
This recording preserves that failure.

29
00:01:56,865 --> 00:02:03,167
The repository separately contains successful isolated decline evidence, clearly labelled as a scripted model rehearsal.

30
00:02:03,567 --> 00:02:11,819
The earlier live memory demonstration links D P fourteen to a later investigation of D P seventeen for the same synthetic customer.

31
00:02:11,819 --> 00:02:18,196
H MEM recalls a candidate, and Zetaris verifies the original committed receipt before the investigator sees it.

32
00:02:18,196 --> 00:02:23,448
The later case received a fifty seven dollar sixty cent simulated credit under policy.

33
00:02:23,448 --> 00:02:25,323
Memory is advisory and partial.

34
00:02:25,323 --> 00:02:30,200
The pinned reference uses mock embeddings, and memory retries cannot execute an action.

35
00:02:30,600 --> 00:02:34,403
A fresh public checkout reproduced two isolated rehearsal cycles.

36
00:02:34,403 --> 00:02:38,207
Each produced eight decisions, four credits, and one review.

37
00:02:38,207 --> 00:02:45,391
The cases cover all four outcomes, duplicate prevention, one injected amount correction, and the policy version boundary.

38
00:02:45,391 --> 00:02:52,153
These runs use real disposable PostgreSQL and the pinned H MEM reference, with scripted model responses.

39
00:02:52,153 --> 00:02:55,533
They do not call live Zetaris or Nightshift.

40
00:02:55,933 --> 00:03:06,151
The repository includes dated live sponsor evidence and two hundred and sixty seven main tests plus sixteen reference checks that passed in the full verification matrix.

41
00:03:06,151 --> 00:03:09,688
Nightshift response metadata reported the Nemotron model shown here.

42
00:03:09,688 --> 00:03:13,225
That label is recorded evidence, not independent provider attestation.

43
00:03:13,225 --> 00:03:18,333
Setup instructions include a clean checkout route and a separately configured live route.

44
00:03:18,733 --> 00:03:22,653
This is a local reference demo using synthetic documents.

45
00:03:22,653 --> 00:03:30,491
It currently has one PostgreSQL datasource, no universal semantic layer, and one model investigator with a deterministic critic.

46
00:03:30,491 --> 00:03:34,411
Broader evidence handling and production controls remain future work.

47
00:03:34,411 --> 00:03:39,637
The public submission package includes the deck, video, transcript, architecture, and evidence.

48
00:03:39,637 --> 00:03:45,733
The team leader still needs to verify portal requirements and complete the final submission.
